      'from.australia.faq.q2': 'Can I attach documents?',
      'from.australia.faq.q3': 'What types of documents do people typically send?',
      'from.australia.faq.a0': 'Yes. Payment goes through Stripe in Canadian dollars, any major credit or debit card works, including Australian cards. Your bank handles the AUD to CAD conversion.',
      'from.australia.faq.a1': 'We print and mail within one business day of payment. Canada Post standard lettermail then delivers within Canada in up to 2 weeks.',
      'from.australia.faq.a2': 'Yes, up to 5 PDF or Word files, 10 MB each. All printed in full colour and included in the envelope.',
      'from.australia.faq.a3': 'Letters to family, cards, immigration paperwork, tax forms, legal correspondence, and signed contracts are all common. As long as it\'s printable and fits in an envelope, we can send it.',
      'from.australia.postage.p1': 'Sending a letter directly from Australia to Canada via Australia Post costs around <strong>AUD $3.50</strong> for a standard international letter (up to 50g) in 2026. Delivery is generally 10–25 business days through the international mail network, with no tracking on standard letters.',
      'from.australia.postage.p2': 'By comparison, Letterhome mails your letter from <em>inside</em> Canada for <strong>$10 CAD</strong>, it skips the international leg entirely and travels as domestic Canadian lettermail. Delivery within Canada is typically up to 2 weeks from the date it\'s posted, and your letter arrives with a Canadian mailing date.',
      'from.australia.cta.btn': 'Send a letter from Australia →',
      'from.bangladesh.eyebrow': 'Mailing from Bangladesh',
      'from.bangladesh.h1': 'Send mail to Canada from Bangladesh',
      'from.bangladesh.lede': 'Need to mail a letter or document to Canada from Bangladesh? We handle the printing, the Canadian postage, and the trip to the post office, so you don\'t have to.',
