      'from.brazil.faq.q1': 'Can I send immigration documents to Canada from Brazil?',
      'from.brazil.faq.q2': 'How long will it take for my letter to arrive?',
      'from.brazil.faq.q3': 'What types of documents can I send?',
      'from.brazil.faq.a0': 'We charge in Canadian dollars ($10 CAD) processed through Stripe. Your card will convert at your bank\'s exchange rate, no Brazilian account required.',
      'from.brazil.faq.a1': 'Yes. Upload your PDFs, enter the Canadian mailing address, and we handle everything: printing, enveloping, and mailing from within Canada.',
      'from.brazil.faq.a2': 'We mail within one business day of payment. Canada Post standard lettermail then delivers within Canada in up to 2 weeks.',
      'from.brazil.faq.a3': 'Any document you can save as a PDF or Word file: letters, legal forms, immigration paperwork, financial documents, personal correspondence.',
      'from.brazil.postage.p1': 'Sending a standard letter from Brazil to Canada via Correios costs approximately <strong>BRL 8–18</strong> (roughly US$1.50–3.50). Delivery typically takes <strong>2–6 weeks</strong>. Registered international mail with tracking is available but costs more. DHL and FedEx offer faster courier service at US$25–60 for a small envelope.',
      'from.brazil.postage.p2': 'With Letterhome, your letter is printed and mailed from <em>inside</em> Canada for <strong>$10 CAD</strong> (approximately BRL 38). It goes through Canada Post\'s domestic network, no customs, no international delays, typically arriving within Canada in up to 2 weeks.',
      'from.brazil.cta.btn': 'Send a letter from Brazil &rarr;',
      'from.cameroon.eyebrow': 'Guide',
      'from.cameroon.h1': '🇨🇲 Send a letter from Cameroon to Canada',
